 "text": "Hey, good to hear from you. Are you doing okay? Nice of you. Her age, her likes and fears, or lack of them, give you pretty clear hints. Then something with pad and dry erase pencils is sure bet. A small sketchbook would be about right in size too. Stickers she can remove, and small toys she can stop running at room from, are good. A stuffed animal that actually stays still is the easiest to use. Then use it first, it gives both of her the confidence that the gift won't disappear. A small tote bag is valuable in so many ways. She' carry her drawing stuff, her lunch, and maybe a little tissue paper",
